  "short": "Allowance to help stabilize the lives of single-parent and similar families",
  "target": "Single parents or other guardians raising a child (until the end of the fiscal year in which the child turns 18, or under age 20 if the child has a certain disability) who does not share a livelihood with their father or mother due to divorce, death, a certain disability, abandonment, a DV protection order, incarceration, or similar circumstances. An income limit applies, and depending on income, the allowance is paid in full, in part, or not at all",
  "benefit": "Monthly amounts from the April 2026 (Reiwa 8) payment: for the first child, 48,050 yen (full payment) or 48,040 yen to 11,340 yen (partial payment). For each second and subsequent child, an additional 11,350 yen (full payment) or 11,340 yen to 5,680 yen (partial payment) is added. This reflects a 3.2% increase based on the national consumer price index for 2025 (Reiwa 7) (up 3.2% from the previous year). Paid in odd-numbered months (January, March, May, July, September, and November), two months' worth at a time, 6 times a year",
