  "short": "Living-cost benefit for single parents while training for qualifications",
  "target": "Single parents (mothers of single-mother families or fathers of single-father families) who receive the Child Rearing Allowance or have an equivalent income level, who study at a training institution with a curriculum of 6 months or longer to obtain a qualification such as nurse, childcare worker, or certified care worker, and for whom balancing study with work or childcare is recognized as difficult. Private qualifications in digital and other fields (with courses covered by education and training benefits as the standard) may also be eligible",
