  "target": "People in a state of hikikomori (social withdrawal) and their families (any age; at stages when the person themselves cannot yet take action, families can consult on their own)",
  "benefit": "Free consultation support is available from hikikomori support coordinators holding qualifications such as certified social worker, psychiatric social worker, public health nurse, licensed psychologist, or clinical psychologist. Centers also provide referrals to local organizations (medical care, welfare, employment support, and more) and information. At the municipal level, the \"Hikikomori Support Station\" program, which provides consultation support, places to belong, and community networks, is also spreading (129 local governments in FY2025)",
